c7e3c-0d0e-5c12-afc8-020d832fd510" :question/math-academy-id "q-130621" :question/problem "If $K=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}]$, then ${K}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${K}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & =K\\cdot K \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${K}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $K$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${K}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & ={K}^{2}\\cdot {K}^{2} \\\\  & =O\\cdot O \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{4}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184160 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b51e8ff1-247b-5efd-a684-8fca6c064e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c8fc809-c7c8-51da-97a9-cd29d45be4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421534} {:answer/id #uuid "35223ea7-957d-558a-abed-700d6db7d746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421535} {:answer/id #uuid "3f394fb3-e71c-5ca8-9f2c-6be2526c01f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421536} {:answer/id #uuid "60dea114-5917-5702-91f4-2d9dcc51d500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421537} {:answer/id #uuid "d7328dc6-408b-5e04-a91b-4f561c57f94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35223ea7-957d-558a-abed-700d6db7d746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421535} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd431940-6ae8-53c2-934a-5aaba85bb3f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e78f486a-816c-52d1-9895-59ae0c720ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130635" :question/problem "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]$, then ${B}^{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${B}^{2}=B,$ so $B$ is an idempotent matrix. \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${B}^{5}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{5} & ={B}^{2}\\cdot {B}^{2}\\cdot B \\\\  & =B\\cdot B\\cdot B \\\\  & ={B}^{2}\\cdot B \\\\  & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & ={B}^{2} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{B}^{5}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc8dc1a1-9606-5b67-942e-219ab2ddfc1c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Nilpotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d3b2e